1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:03,060
America and Britain almost went to war.

2
00:00:03,080 --> 00:00:04,760
Over one pig.

3
00:00:04,860 --> 00:00:07,200
A farmer caught it eating his potatoes.

4
00:00:07,220 --> 00:00:08,560
So he shot it.

5
00:00:08,580 --> 00:00:08,980
Problem:

6
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:10,693
the farmer was American.

7
00:00:10,713 --> 00:00:12,605
The pig was British.

8
00:00:12,720 --> 00:00:14,015
He offered ten dollars.

9
00:00:14,035 --> 00:00:16,090
The owner wanted a hundred.

10
00:00:16,110 --> 00:00:18,880
Worse, both countries claimed the island.

11
00:00:18,900 --> 00:00:21,840
America sent over four hundred soldiers.

12
00:00:21,860 --> 00:00:23,895
Britain sent five warships.

13
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:26,322
The governor wanted the Americans gone.

14
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:27,970
The admiral said no.

15
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:29,620
Not over a pig.

16
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,439
So both sides just stayed.

17
00:00:31,459 --> 00:00:33,510
For twelve years.

18
00:00:33,530 --> 00:00:34,780
And partied together.

19
00:00:34,800 --> 00:00:36,960
Then a German emperor settled it.

20
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,820
The island went to America.

21
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,050
Total casualties:

22
00:00:40,070 --> 00:00:41,130
one pig.

23
00:00:41,220 --> 00:00:43,270
Team farmer, or team pig?
